# ============================================================================
# Supabase & Local Services
# ============================================================================
.supabase/
rabbitmq_data/
redis_data/
# Local dev seed data. It carries a dev password, so the TEMPLATE (seed.sql.example)
# is what gets committed, never this file. Supabase runs supabase/seed.sql after all
# migrations, on `supabase start` and on every `supabase db reset`.
supabase/seed.sql
# Supabase CLI scratch (`supabase/.branches`, `supabase/.temp`) is ignored by
# `supabase/.gitignore`, which the CLI generates and which owns the CLI's own
# artifacts. Those two files used to be tracked because the only rules lived in
# this repo's former sibling; an ignore rule never untracks a tracked file, so
# `git rm --cached` did that part.

# ============================================================================
# Agent tool local state (caches / possible credentials) — never tracked
# ============================================================================
.kilo/
.kilocode/
.commandcode/
.hallmark/
.minimax/
.qwen/
.claude/

